.SH NAME
le-ready - Block until something starts listening (open-when-ready)


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBle ready  [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Block until something is listening on \&. With --timeout, give up
after that long and exit non-zero.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for ready

.PP
\fB-t\fP, \fB--timeout\fP=0s
	give up after this long (e.g. 30s); 0 waits forever


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBle(1)\fP


